  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>To form product [C] multiple name reactions are taking place.</p><p>To form product [A] when aromatic amine react with nitrous acid it forms diazonium salt which when treated with copper salts as reagent forms aryl halides and reaction is called as Sendmeyer reaction.</p><p>Now product [A] that is when treated with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;in presence of sunlight, free radical substitution takes place and [B] is formed.</p><p>Now when [B] is treated with sodium metal in presence of dry ether forms product [B] by Wurtz reaction.</p><p>Overall reaction takes place as:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0150_9f13a2769cb5.png\" style=\"width: 542px; height: 322px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>"
